# Git LFS was retired on 2026-09-22.
#
# The audio test fixtures under testdata/audio/ were the only reason LFS
# existed here: ~1.8 GB of LibriVox recordings. Every CI job fetched all of it
# on checkout -- 23 checkout steps across 13 workflows, none of which read
# testdata/audio -- which cost roughly 36 GB of LFS bandwidth per pull-request
# push and exhausted the repository's LFS budget, failing every job before any
# project code ran.
#
# Those fixtures are now fetched on demand from archive.org, pinned by sha256:
# see testdata/audio/manifest.json and scripts/fetch_fixtures.py, or run
# `make fixtures`. They are gitignored, so nothing large re-enters the repo.
#
# testdata/fixtures/test_sample.{mp3,m4b,flac} stay committed as ordinary
# files. They total 11.6 KB, and a dozen tests want them on every checkout.

# Media are binary: never newline-normalize them.
*.m4b -text
*.m4a -text
*.mp3 -text
*.flac -text
*.webm -text
*.png -text
